From 94922e363516e540e67ef28e546b42f1e6aa73af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ozgur Guzeldereli <ozgur@guzeldereli.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 19:19:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] CUDA decode fusions for qwen35 DeltaNet layers; indexed
 reader checks

- gdn gates: the beta (mul_mat [+add] sigmoid) and gate (mul_mat add softplus
  mul) chains of a DeltaNet layer as one kernel (k_gdn_gates).
- l2 norm of q / k (scale(rms_norm(x))) folded into the gated_delta_net kernel
  when the state is gathered.
- output norm: rms_norm * w * silu(z) as one kernel (k_gdn_out_norm).
- The fusion checks for readers outside the matched nodes used a scan of the
  whole graph per candidate (quadratic host time each graph evaluation: 29 tok/s
  without CUDA graphs). A per-evaluation reader count index makes each check
  O(matched nodes).

27B TQ1_P on an RTX 3090 Ti, tg128: 94.3 -> 99.1 tok/s (88.5 without CUDA
graphs, was 29); KLD vs the unfused decode 1.43e-4, same top token 99.35%.
Each fusion can be turned off: GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_GDN_GATES / _GDN_L2 /
_GDN_OUT_NORM.
